### Dot directories: DENY EVERYTHING, allow back what has to exist ###
# Owner ruling (2026-07-29): "would it not be easier to ignore every directory path starting with
# '.', and keep only the ones that really have to exist? That stops agents from dumping things by
# accident, and stops you from cleaning up after them, without blocking them."
#
# It inverts the problem: instead of chasing each new scratch name an agent invents -- a list that
# only grows after the mess -- the set is denied and the two dot directories this tree tracks are
# deliberately allowed back.
#
# `.*/` matches DIRECTORIES only (trailing slash), at any depth. Dot FILES at the root
# (`.gitattributes`, `.gitignore`) are untouched, and `.claude/worktrees/` needs a rule of its own
# because `worktrees` does not start with a dot.
.*/
!.claude/
!.github/

### Host configs derived from `teko.toml` ###
# `mc.macos.toml`, `mc.ci.toml` and `mc.<fixture>.toml` are born from a `sed` over the versioned
# `teko.toml` (the build config) and are transient to one host or one loop -- never a source. The
# versioned ones are `teko.toml` (build) and `mc.toml` (the package manifest, `[package]` only);
# both stay out of this rule.
/mc.*.toml
!/mc.toml

# agent worktrees / session temporaries -- never versioned
scratchpad/

### The website (site/README.md) ###
# `mcsite` rebuilds site/public from scratch on every run, so it is generated,
# never committed; `_mc/` is the shallow checkout of minicompiler/mc that the
# generator is built from when the site is rendered locally.
site/public/
_mc/
